    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Junior Caminero** (73.35) headlining our offensive attack. **Yelich** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Imai (5.17 xERA) and an ideal leadoff spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. Similarly, **Caminero** is perfectly positioned in the cleanup hole against Kochanowicz; the combination of a favorable SP projection and a +4% boost from his batting order creates an elite environment for power production. We also see high-ceiling value from **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Colt Keith** (63.27), both of whom are projected to thrive from leadoff spots and advantageous platoon splits against their respective right-handed opponents.\n\nWhile we are chasing points, we must account for the volatility introduced by elite opposing arms. **Trea Turner** (50.91) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.24) face Yamamoto, whose 3.33 xERA serves as a significant drag on their output. Despite the prestige of these names, their efficiency scores are hampered by the high-skill SP matchup, forcing them to the bottom of our starting hierarchy. The closest call on the bench was **Chase Meidroth** (50.42); while he maintains a solid projection against Montero, the crowded middle-infield options of **Caleb Durbin** and **Colt Keith** offered higher situational stability, ultimately relegating **Meidroth** to a reserve role. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (57.16) start closely; despite his elite speed upside, he faces a left-on-left disadvantage that dragged his score down by 15%\u2014a situational risk that bears watching should his early at-bats prove unproductive. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in starter despite his middling 55.68 score, as his elite xwOBA (0.424) provides a secondary floor that the raw projection metrics cannot fully capture. We remain without **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hyeseong Kim** due to injury and minor league status, leaving our depth options like **Carson Benge** on standby should any late-inning weather or lineup changes necessitate a defensive swap.",
